## Authentication
API Key (x-goog-api-key) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Data Read (2)
- `GET /api/v1/apps/{appId}/cross-app/details` — Get details for cross-app data.
- `GET /ds-data/ads/active/v5` — Get active ad data.

### Data Write (2)
- `POST /api/event` — Report an event.
- `POST /v1/projects/{projectId}/installations` — Register a project installation.

### Media (2)
- `GET /a/direct/{id}/native/{id}` — Retrieve native media content.
- `GET /cms/images/{imageId}` — Retrieve an image from CMS.

### Config (1)
- `GET /{id}/projects/-/apps/1:592900011890:web:6c46b518a66d5656548feb/webconfig` — Retrieve web app configuration.

